PeaZip is an OS-portable file archiver. Features archive volume
spanning, compression, authenticated encryption. Supports .7z and 7-zip
sfx self-extracting archives, BZip2, GZip, pea, tar, Z, zip and raw
split/join file with optional integrity check.
Input file lists, job definitions and job reports can be saved to have
full control of archiving-related operations or to be used in scripts.
PeaZip is released under LGPL for Windows and Linux (GTK1 and GTK2).
Interface is fully skinnable and skins can be saved as plain text; on
Windows 2000 and XP it uses adjustable transparence level.
SourceForge project page: https://sourceforge.net/projects/peazip/
Website: http://peazip.sourceforge.net/

Release notes 1.1:
This update is focused in giving the program more usability, through
many UI improvements.
Windows version now runs fine also on 9x systems; most used functions
as add to archive or extract here are accessible from shortcuts in
SendTo menu; Windows installer now asks for optionally creating
additional file associations.
>From links in SendTo menu it's possible to directly send from Explorer
multiple files and folders to archives of different types, encrypt,
split files and it is possible to extract, extract to new folder, test
or list multiple archives at once, even of mixed types.
For Linux is now available also a GTK2 build, offering better look and
feel and more usable system dialogs; both Linux versions (GTK1 and
GTK2) are standalone binaries, you just need to unpack and run them.

